  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "What is the value of $f(t)=\u27e8\\frac{4}{t-1},\\,1+{t}^{3},\\,(t-1)^{4}\u27e9$ at $t=3?$",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $t=3$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) & =\u27e8\\frac{4}{3-1},1+{3}^{3},(3-1)^{4}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{4}{2},1+27,{2}^{4}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82,28,16\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(t)$ at $t=3$ is the vector $\u27e82,28,16\u27e9.$",
